From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 21:40:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec: build a second H.264 decoder for MVC, h264_mvc, next
 to the stock one

H.264 MVC is how a Blu-ray 3D carries its two eyes: a base view that any
H.264 decoder plays and a second view predicted from it. FFmpeg does not
decode the second view. A series that adds it to the H.264 decoder
(Dom Cobley, FFmpeg pull request 24303) is not merged; it changes the
decoder that every H.264 stream goes through.

Here that series is applied to a copy of the decoder's sources, which
the build of this package generates into libavcodec/h264mvc/ (the
recipe's post_patch hook, h264-mvc/twin.sh), and the copy is built as a
decoder of its own, h264_mvc: a software decoder, with every global
symbol under another name. This patch is all that the stock files get:
the decoder is declared after the stock one, so that the stock one stays
the decoder that is found for the codec, it selects the same parts, and
the Makefile of the new folder is included.

The parts of the series for other files of FFmpeg than the decoder's
(the H.264 parser, the mov demuxer, the extract_extradata bitstream
filter, documentation and tests) are not applied: they would change
stock code. What that leaves out: FFmpeg gives the decoder no parameter
sets of the second view that a file has only in an 'mvcC' box. A player
can: the decoder reads them from the 'avcC' record that it is opened
with (Kodi puts them there for a Matroska file, which has that box
behind the record). An MP4 file, whose box the series teaches the mov
demuxer to read, plays its base view. A stream that has those sets
among its NAL units is decoded with both views either way.

Checked on a host build of this source, with the series as of
2026-10-14 (Dom Cobley's branch at b72a935c6c28) carried to FFmpeg
9.0.2: it is written for a later FFmpeg, and where its context names
what only that FFmpeg has (H.264 data partitioning, a check that 9.0.2
does not have, the layout of the Changelog and of three test references)
it takes the form of 9.0.2; its own changes are as he wrote them. The
20 objects of the stock decoder, its parser and what the two decoders
share are the same bytes with and without the new decoder (without
debug information, which names the folder); FFmpeg's own H.264 tests
pass (209, with one thread, frame threads and slice threads); h264_mvc
used as a plain H.264 decoder gives the output of the stock one in the
205 of those tests that give frames; and of the ITU-T H.264.1 MVC
conformance streams, the base view of all 27 and the second view of 18
of the 19 that the reference decoder (JM 19.1) gives one for are
identical to the reference decoder's output, with one thread, frame
threads and slice threads. The one that differs is MVCDS-6_old, a
superseded stream, whose replacement MVCDS-6 has the same structure
and is identical; why the old one differs is not known. Two streams
made for this with the reference encoder (Stereo High, 1920x1080 and
960x540) are identical to the reference decoder in both views, with one
thread, with frame threads (8, and 16 for the second) and with slice
threads.
---
 configure              | 2 ++
 libavcodec/Makefile    | 1 +
 libavcodec/allcodecs.c | 1 +
 3 files changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/configure b/configure
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -3219,6 +3219,8 @@
 h263p_encoder_select="h263_encoder"
 h264_decoder_select="cabac golomb h264chroma h264dsp h264parse h264pred h264qpel h264_sei videodsp"
 h264_decoder_suggest="error_resilience"
+h264_mvc_decoder_select="cabac golomb h264chroma h264dsp h264parse h264pred h264qpel h264_sei videodsp"
+h264_mvc_decoder_suggest="error_resilience"
 hap_decoder_select="snappy texturedsp"
 hap_encoder_deps="libsnappy"
 hap_encoder_select="texturedspenc"
diff --git a/libavcodec/Makefile b/libavcodec/Makefile
--- a/libavcodec/Makefile
+++ b/libavcodec/Makefile
@@ -70,6 +70,7 @@
 # subsystems
 include $(SRC_PATH)/libavcodec/aac/Makefile
 include $(SRC_PATH)/libavcodec/hevc/Makefile
+include $(SRC_PATH)/libavcodec/h264mvc/Makefile
 include $(SRC_PATH)/libavcodec/opus/Makefile
 include $(SRC_PATH)/libavcodec/vvc/Makefile
 include $(SRC_PATH)/libavcodec/vulkan/Makefile
diff --git a/libavcodec/allcodecs.c b/libavcodec/allcodecs.c
--- a/libavcodec/allcodecs.c
+++ b/libavcodec/allcodecs.c
@@ -148,6 +148,7 @@
 extern const FFCodec ff_h263p_decoder;
 extern const FFCodec ff_h263_v4l2m2m_decoder;
 extern const FFCodec ff_h264_decoder;
+extern const FFCodec ff_h264_mvc_decoder;
 extern const FFCodec ff_h264_v4l2m2m_decoder;
 extern const FFCodec ff_h264_mediacodec_decoder;
 extern const FFCodec ff_h264_mediacodec_encoder;
